From: postmarketOS mojito port
Subject: [PATCH] pmdomain: qcom: rpmhpd: add MSS to qcs615

qcom_q6v5_pas attaches the cx and mss proxy domains for the modem; without MSS the attach fails
with -ENODATA. Patch 0013 of github.com/VipinVIP/violet-sm6150-mainline (MIT), unchanged.
---
diff --git a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
index 919efa34e..55442cc4c 100644
--- a/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/qcom/rpmhpd.c
@@ -912,6 +912,14 @@ static const struct rpmhpd_desc qcs8300_desc = {
 static struct rpmhpd *qcs615_rpmhpds[] = {
 	[RPMHPD_CX] = &cx,
 	[RPMHPD_CX_AO] = &cx_ao,
+	/*
+	 * The modem (mpss) votes on the MSS rail: qcom_q6v5_pas's
+	 * mpss_resource_init attaches proxy power domains "cx" and "mss", and
+	 * without this entry qcom_pas_pds_attach() fails with -ENODATA, which
+	 * is what has kept mpss - and therefore the WLAN firmware bootstrap -
+	 * off on violet.
+	 */
+	[RPMHPD_MSS] = &mss,
 };
 
 static const struct rpmhpd_desc qcs615_desc = {
